{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931290Z","id":"1f1d83cfddbe3c98907366125e5d52e3977219be9dc8e4a5140d4306eade3a91","body":{"detail":"In the derive branch of `share_explicit`, `record_artifact` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:842-844) writes the cache record under `derived.provenance.id`, which the derivers normalise: Claude uses the session-chain head (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:52-61, a successor-segment id maps to the head), Gemini uses `session_uuid` over the entry id (derive.rs:122-128), Codex resolves a partial UUID prefix to the rollout's full id (derive.rs:162-169, toolpath-codex `find_rollout_file` accepts a substring match at crates/toolpath-codex/src/paths.rs:118-130). `record_remotes` at cmd_share.rs:877-884 passes `session` instead, so `path share --session <successor|prefix|entry id>` leaves the cache record under one key and inserts a second known-but-uncached entry under the raw id via `record_remote`'s `or_insert_with` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:110-125). Sync enumerates only the normalised id, so the stray entry is never materialised, and the chain-head entry that incremental append / `share --all` will consult carries no remote. The fast path (cmd_share.rs:784-789) is unaffected because `fresh_cache_id` only matches when `session` is already the manifest key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":873},"end":{"line":884},"content_hash":"5cda0306fb41a83e9e37d7c071cb05d728ac1a23de8819cd8f605e89aa58dabc"},"suggested_fix":"In the derive branch, record under `derived.provenance.as_ref().map(|p| (p.id.as_str(), p.path.as_deref()))`, falling back to `session`/`project` only when provenance is `None`; add a share test that passes a Claude successor-segment id (or a Codex prefix) and asserts the remote lands on the same entry as `cache_id`.","summary":"Derive-path share records the remote under the caller's `session` id, not the manifest id the cache record uses","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931385Z","id":"afcb76e8987fa3d8800c76ef780ea1e43ed552db89a78503307f89fa5987a827","body":{"detail":"`project_into_harness` collapses `ClaudeProjection::Written` and `ClaudeProjection::AlreadyLocal` into one `session_id` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:677-683); `AlreadyLocal` means the local file was left untouched and 'may be newer than the shared document' (crates/path-cli/src/projection/claude.rs:10-13, 26-30). `record_pull` (cmd_resume.rs:223-285) then stats that untouched local file for `source_stamp` (lines 266-268) while `steps`/`last_step`/`head` come from the fetched path (line 269). The spec's stat gate skips a session whose stamp has not moved, so steps the local session already has beyond the fetched prefix would count as sent. `record_remote` replaces any earlier record at the URL (engine.rs:126), so a `--force` re-fetch of a session that was shared from this machine overwrites a correct share record with this one. Reproduce: `path share` a session, then `path resume --force <its url>` in the same project.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"341a7cb7862f3ff7023e9ea2fe4da0b07912c38d511c99544db4df827b4434da"},"suggested_fix":"Have `project_into_harness` return whether it wrote the session (or a `Projected { session_id, written: bool }`), and call `record_pull` only when `written` is true; alternatively skip the write when the session's manifest entry already has a record for that URL.","summary":"`record_pull` also runs when projection found an existing local session, pairing the fetched doc's `steps`/`head` with a possibly newer local stamp","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931488Z","id":"7340776360dd09e42bc06cb3f14514f74e02a586bd012fae0287fcf54559f2ae","body":{"detail":"`run_pathbase` reads the cache body at crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:872 and only after the upload returns calls `session_of_cache_id` (line 888), which takes `(rec.modified, rec.size)` from the manifest as it is then (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:483-494). A `p cache sync` (or a `path query` auto-sync) that re-derives the session between those two points rewrites the cache file and the record's stamp (`record_artifact`/`flush_writes`, engine.rs:252-269, 400-422) while the cache id stays the same (it is `make_id(type, path.id)`, derive.rs:84). The remote record then says the remote holds the derive at the new stamp although the old body was uploaded, and the spec's stat gate skips the session until the source moves again. The share paths avoid this by taking the stamp before the read (`fresh_cache_id` at cmd_share.rs:784; `claude_chain_stamp` before `read_conversation` at derive.rs:56-73).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":885},"end":{"line":892},"content_hash":"37405d03890c3001e59d6b5917d8eda946acc829c2d2ee492a1fa4506abbbc0f"},"suggested_fix":"Call `session_of_cache_id(&args.input)` before `std::fs::read_to_string(&file)` and carry the stamp through to `record_remotes`; or re-read it afterwards and skip the record when the two differ.","summary":"`p export pathbase <cache id>` reads the session's stamp after the upload, so a concurrent sync can stamp the record newer than the body that was sent","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931573Z","id":"2486d9fc48552c6fc5b0f95ffb6597973fa8fb4f4978218c4b8e199618ac6988","body":{"detail":"`remote_path_url` interpolates `base_url`, `owner`, `repo` and `graph_id` as given, trimming only a trailing slash. On push `base_url` is the stored credential URL or `resolve_url(--url)` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:951-963) and `graph_id` is `Uuid::to_string()` of the create response (cmd_pathbase.rs:588, lowercase hyphenated). On pull `base_url` is `format!(\"{scheme}{host}\")` from the URL exactly as the user typed it (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:464) and `graph_id` is the raw `ref_.id` segment (cmd_resume.rs:261), which `extract_triple` accepts in any form `Uuid::parse_str` takes (derive.rs:488-491: uppercase, braces, no hyphens). Owner/repo from a URL are not percent-decoded before `encode_segment` re-encodes them (derive.rs:494-501 → cmd_pathbase.rs:84-86), so an already-encoded segment is double-encoded. Example: `path share` records `https://pathbase.dev/u/me/r/graphs/fe94b6f9-.../paths/...`; `path resume https://PATHBASE.DEV/u/me/r/graphs/FE94B6F9-.../` records a second key for the same path. The client base also differs from the server's `public_url` whenever the client reaches the server through another host (the server's own URL for the graph is `created.url`, pathbase `crates/pathbase-api/src/responses.rs:109-112`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"a6caa163c5805bc004c314d4b0fe25641f3439e9d58a3954af30c52f8786bfda"},"suggested_fix":"Canonicalise inside `remote_path_url`: lowercase scheme and host, take the graph id as a `uuid::Uuid` (both call sites already have one) and render it with `to_string()`, and percent-decode URL segments in `extract_triple` before they are re-encoded. Add a test that the key from a typed-URL pull equals the key from a credential-URL push for the same graph.","summary":"Push and pull build the record key from differently-normalised inputs, so one path can get two keys","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931631Z","id":"c1304b44445471c14d4a19295c87809a9b1446e016409bd637962e2a029261e9","body":{"detail":"`resolve_input` sets `fetched` only in the network branch (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:453); the cache-hit branch (lines 431-440) leaves it `None`, and `run_with_strategy` records nothing (lines 210-212). The projected Claude session id is derived from the path, not minted per run (crates/path-cli/src/projection/claude.rs:25-35), so a second `path resume <url>` in the same project resolves to `AlreadyLocal` and keeps the first run's record; but the same URL resumed in a different project directory, or any harness whose projection mints a fresh id, produces a new session with no `remotes` entry. The spec (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-path-parent-and-delegation-design.md § Remote records, pathbase repo) says a pull creates the record so that 'work done in the resumed session then appends to that path instead of creating a new graph'; for every resume after the first that outcome does not hold. Only the server id lookup needs the network, and `graph_paths_list` is already a separate call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":431},"end":{"line":440},"content_hash":"d6d66a3575f7e8d794be1d06381503914a7dba4bab5ab8a8700b9221e3f11a1a"},"suggested_fix":"Record on cache hits too: set `fetched` in both branches (the cached document still came from `base_url`/`ref_`), and let `record_pull` make its one `GET …/graphs/{id}/paths` request, warning and continuing offline as it already does on error. Add a test for the cached-resume case.","summary":"A resume served from the cache writes no remote record, so a second resume of the same URL into another project cannot append to the path","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931710Z","id":"1476309721fcd6900c43c2d9c968a7ad8546ba46b184b3046871dff6aaadd8f5","body":{"detail":"`relax_for_older_servers` (crates/pathbase-client/build.rs:85-105) makes `GraphCreatedResponse.paths` optional so an older server's response decodes with `paths: []`. `uploaded_paths` then yields an empty list (cmd_export.rs:979-988), and `record_remotes` finds no URL for any path and `continue`s (lines 927-935) without a message. The CHANGELOG entry for 0.30.0 tells users every successful `path share`/`p export pathbase` writes a record; against such a server none is written and nothing says so, and once incremental append reads these records every share against that server will open a new graph. The pull side already warns in the analogous case (`graph_paths_list` returns no match, cmd_resume.rs:253-259).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":910},"end":{"line":942},"content_hash":"61c87f8de46b135d7b6af47ea992010512db50f205955a6cc1103429b9b4e009"},"suggested_fix":"In `record_remotes`, when `doc` has at least one inline path with steps but `uploaded` is empty, `eprintln!` one warning naming the server as not reporting stored paths; the test `share_from_the_cache_records_the_upload` (cmd_share.rs) can assert it.","summary":"An upload whose create response lists no paths records nothing silently; warn when the document had inline paths","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195633Z","id":"25f3a36bb1f187aa8b82bbd9e79d9d38a518534d6cb610ac8146e8026c67dc14","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:871-873 reads the cache body; :885 runs the upload; only then does :888 call `crate::sync::session_of_cache_id(&args.input)`, which returns `(rec.modified, rec.size)` from the manifest as it is at that moment (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:483-494). A concurrent `p cache sync` overwrites the same cache file (`write_cached(&derived.cache_id, ..., true)`, engine.rs:363) and the record's `modified`/`size` (engine.rs:364-377 staged, :253-269 flushed via `put_record` :244-249, which keeps `remotes`), and the cache id is unchanged because it is `make_id(ArtifactType::Claude.name(), &path.path.id)` (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:84). The record written at :891 then carries the newer stamp with the older body's `steps`/`last_step`, and the stat gate (spec: source_stamp skips a session whose stamp has not moved) skips it. `share_explicit` takes the stamp before the read (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:784 `fresh_cache_id`, :871-876 provenance stamp), so the two paths are inconsistent. A timing-dependent race with no deterministic repro: `concern` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"7340776360dd09e42bc06cb3f14514f74e02a586bd012fae0287fcf54559f2ae","summary":"confirmed: the stamp is read from the manifest after the upload, so a sync between the body read and that lookup stamps the record newer than the uploaded body","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195710Z","id":"6f2b7df9c776921f0f9c2be576a8f71dd7a356b6f662b27def389fe8ec53a841","body":{"detail":"crates/pathbase-client/build.rs:91-104 drops `paths` from `GraphCreatedResponse`'s required list, so an older server's response decodes with an empty vector (test `graphs_post_accepts_a_response_without_paths`, crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:1516-1532 asserts `created.paths.is_empty()`). `run_pathbase_inner` returns `uploaded_paths(.., &created.paths)` / `&resp.paths` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:1015, :1086), and `record_remotes` :929-935 `continue`s per path with no output when no URL matches. No warning exists between :910-945, nor in `run_pathbase_inner` :966-1087. The streamed route is unaffected (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:852-857 fills `created.paths` from the per-path open responses), so this is only the `body.len() <= BATCH_BUDGET || !streamable` branch (:1037-1046) and the anon route (:997-1015). CHANGELOG.md:12-14 promises a record after every successful `path share`/`p export pathbase`. `cmd_resume.rs:254-260` does warn in the analogous pull case. Kind `suggestion` fits: nothing breaks today since nothing reads the records yet (engine.rs:60-61).","kind":"comment","references":"1476309721fcd6900c43c2d9c968a7ad8546ba46b184b3046871dff6aaadd8f5","summary":"confirmed: a create response with no `paths` records nothing and prints nothing on the single-request and anonymous routes","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195733Z","id":"931a657b1c34e064b49d32f3cea8c4f5dc0b2ba41bd11f5f189c6492b133488b","body":{"detail":"`remote_path_url` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:73-87) only trims a trailing slash from `base_url` and interpolates `graph_id` as given. Push: `graph_id` is `inner.id.to_string()` of a `format: uuid` field (cmd_pathbase.rs:516, :588; openapi.json `Graph.properties.id` is `{type: string, format: uuid}`), i.e. lowercase hyphenated, and `base_url` is the stored credential URL (cmd_export.rs:957-961). Pull: `parse_pathbase_ref` returns `format!(\"{scheme}{host}\")` with the host exactly as typed (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:450-464, no lowercasing), and `extract_triple` keeps the id segment as a string after only checking `Uuid::parse_str(id).is_err()` (derive.rs:488-491, :509); `Uuid::parse_str` accepts simple, hyphenated, braced and `urn:uuid:` forms (https://docs.rs/uuid/latest/uuid/struct.Uuid.html#method.parse_str). `record_pull` passes that raw `&ref_.id` to `remote_path_url` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:261) even though `graph_paths_list` parses it to a `Uuid` for the request one line earlier (cmd_pathbase.rs:1122-1126). Owner/repo segments are never percent-decoded (derive.rs:494-510) before `encode_segment` re-encodes them (cmd_pathbase.rs:84-85). So `path resume https://PATHBASE.DEV/u/me/r/graphs/FE94B6F9-.../` yields a different key than the push for the same path. Nothing reads the keys yet, so no user-visible failure before merge: `concern` is right.","kind":"comment","references":"2486d9fc48552c6fc5b0f95ffb6597973fa8fb4f4978218c4b8e199618ac6988","summary":"confirmed: pull keys use the typed URL's host and raw graph-id segment while push keys use the credential URL and `Uuid::to_string()`, so the same path can get two keys","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195747Z","id":"b8ef116eec3022bd181ed2ff5ca6a9771b9b56500d369d2516a1a7f6697d94ad","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:209-212 calls `record_pull` whenever `fetched` is set, regardless of how `project_into_harness` resolved; :676-683 collapse `Written` and `AlreadyLocal` into one `session_id`. `AlreadyLocal` means nothing was written and the local copy 'may be newer than the shared document' (crates/path-cli/src/projection/claude.rs:7-14, :26-30). `record_pull` then stats the local session (cmd_resume.rs:266-268) and takes `steps`/`last_step`/`head` from the fetched `path` (:269, `RemoteRecord::of`), and `record_remote` does `remotes.insert(url, record)`, replacing any earlier record under that URL (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:109-131). The projected session id is the original session id carried in the artifact key (`claude-code://<session>`, crates/toolpath-convo/src/extract.rs:139-146 sets `view.id`), so `path share` of session X followed by `path resume --force <its url>` in the same project resolves to `AlreadyLocal { X }` and overwrites X's share record with one whose `steps` is the fetched prefix but whose stamp is the current local file's. Only matters once incremental append reads the records (engine.rs:60-61), so `concern` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"afcb76e8987fa3d8800c76ef780ea1e43ed552db89a78503307f89fa5987a827","summary":"confirmed: `record_pull` runs for `AlreadyLocal` too, pairing the fetched path's steps with the untouched local file's stamp and replacing any share record at that URL","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195759Z","id":"7c55e64db6d5f732a1f0b69a46f404e4467cacd41813762ec9c8c3beb55205e4","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:421 initialises `fetched = None`; the cache-hit branch :431-440 returns the cached JSON without touching it; only the network branch sets it (:453). `run_with_strategy` records only `if let Some(fetched) = &fetched` (:210-212). The projected Claude session id is a function of the path (crates/toolpath-convo/src/extract.rs:139-146; crates/path-cli/src/projection/claude.rs:25-35), so resuming the same URL in a different project directory takes the `Written` branch (claude.rs:26-35, the session file does not exist under that project dir) and the new session has no `remotes` entry. The spec requires a pull to create the record so that work in the resumed session 'appends to that path instead of creating a new graph' (/Users/ben/empathic/oss/pathbase/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-path-parent-and-delegation-design.md:246-250). `record_pull` only needs `base_url`/`ref_`, both available in the cache-hit branch (:429), and its one request is `graph_paths_list` (:237-243) with an offline warning path (:249-252). Nothing consumes the records yet, so `concern` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"c1304b44445471c14d4a19295c87809a9b1446e016409bd637962e2a029261e9","summary":"confirmed: the cache-hit branch leaves `fetched` as `None`, so a resume served from the cache writes no remote record","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195774Z","id":"ef7afc3bcabc31c32c033ee977893336d1cfdbae9d5cc61e49969261a6e436d4","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:842-844 calls `record_artifact(&config, stub, &derived.cache_id)` with `stub = derived.provenance`, whose `id` the derivers normalise: Claude to the chain head (`session_chain(..).into_iter().next()`, crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:56-61, :90), Gemini to `session_uuid` over the entry id (derive.rs:120-128), Codex to the full id of the matched rollout file (derive.rs:162-169). `record_remotes` at cmd_share.rs:877-884 passes `session` instead. `record_remote` keys the manifest by that `id` and `or_insert_with` creates a known-but-uncached `SyncRecord` when it is absent (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:117-131), so a share by a non-canonical id yields two entries: the canonical one with `cache_id` and no remotes, and a stray one with the remote and `cache_id: None`. The fast path is unaffected since `fresh_cache_id` looks up `manifest.get(type)?.get(id)?` by the caller's id and needs `cache_id` (engine.rs:468-469). Kind `concern` fits: the upload succeeds and nothing reads the records yet.","kind":"comment","references":"1f1d83cfddbe3c98907366125e5d52e3977219be9dc8e4a5140d4306eade3a91","summary":"confirmed: the derive branch records the cache under `derived.provenance.id` but the remote under the caller's raw `session`, which differ for successor-segment, entry and prefix ids","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-08T15:38:42.747682Z","id":"241a132d8a30a28cf9fa61328d6616f8e9ce080dd34ffcbb15a22ec971df8e9c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6daa69f","summary":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:880: the derive branch calls record_remotes with the provenance's id and path, the key record_artifact used; test cmd_share::tests::share_by_a_successor_id_records_on_the_chain_head shows a share by a successor id lands on the chain head with no stray entry","supersedes":"1f1d83cfddbe3c98907366125e5d52e3977219be9dc8e4a5140d4306eade3a91","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e986c759-7622-40c8-8cf5-541f4dfb3f97"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-08T15:38:42.791187Z","id":"3a177cac80fe657e37b3e94d0317e26999f16646d6827c75f3776158681541c1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a453378","summary":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:877: run_pathbase calls session_of_cache_id before read_to_string and records with that stamp after the upload; test cmd_export::tests::pathbase_export_stamps_the_record_before_reading_the_body re-stamps the manifest between the open and the body and the record keeps the earlier stamp","supersedes":"7340776360dd09e42bc06cb3f14514f74e02a586bd012fae0287fcf54559f2ae","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e986c759-7622-40c8-8cf5-541f4dfb3f97"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-08T15:38:42.834593Z","id":"660f6d3530756faa7c060c81c1ae44203a65066cccb20f8bbb0a9adb4d8feaf4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:302de37","summary":"record_pull removed with its callers (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs no longer has record_pull or ResolvedInput.fetched); a resume writes no remote record at all, so no AlreadyLocal pairing can occur. Spec § Remote records: 'Pulling a path from a remote (path resume <url>) writes no record for now: the resumed session is a new session and must not append to the path it was pulled from.'","supersedes":"afcb76e8987fa3d8800c76ef780ea1e43ed552db89a78503307f89fa5987a827","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e986c759-7622-40c8-8cf5-541f4dfb3f97"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-08T15:38:42.878125Z","id":"486d2b9626763e9d7bc7a0141cc6ff4943da429bcf9b2049437f2415adb7daa9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:302de37","summary":"Pull writes nothing on every branch now: record_pull, ResolvedInput.fetched and graph_paths_list are removed (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs, cmd_pathbase.rs). Spec § Remote records: 'Pulling a path from a remote (path resume <url>) writes no record for now: the resumed session is a new session and must not append to the path it was pulled from.' Linking a pulled session to its origin is the named follow-up.","supersedes":"c1304b44445471c14d4a19295c87809a9b1446e016409bd637962e2a029261e9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e986c759-7622-40c8-8cf5-541f4dfb3f97"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-08T15:38:42.921173Z","id":"0130fd7886c9d075f09c01b828a4f7e75c272889f8db3c5b84b2ba854d73efff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2ae631b","summary":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:75: remote_path_url is the one builder; it lowercases scheme and host, trims the trailing slash, percent-decodes then encodes owner/repo once, and takes graph and path ids as Uuid (CreatedGraph.id and AnonGraphResponse.id are Uuid now); test remote_path_url_is_one_spelling_per_path. Pull-side keys are gone with the pull record.","supersedes":"2486d9fc48552c6fc5b0f95ffb6597973fa8fb4f4978218c4b8e199618ac6988","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e986c759-7622-40c8-8cf5-541f4dfb3f97"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-08T15:38:43.008129Z","id":"377561c518ccfc578ba4d9c641bc9399a952659fb1053f9a701f6781fe541322","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:64ec5f2","summary":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:928: record_remotes prints 'warning: remote record not written: the server did not list the stored paths' when uploaded is empty and the document had an inline path with steps","supersedes":"1476309721fcd6900c43c2d9c968a7ad8546ba46b184b3046871dff6aaadd8f5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e986c759-7622-40c8-8cf5-541f4dfb3f97"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:09:47.969705Z","id":"8dc2b7a040e666ef7f911c551f6c2cd0a44b2701fb83d4c30b78a0b8363e54bc","body":{"detail":"The test runs `share_explicit` twice on an unchanged session and checks that the second run records the path. It never shows that the second run uploaded from the cache (the `fresh_cache_id` branch at cmd_share.rs:783-825). If that branch were skipped (for example, `fresh_cache_id` returning `None` after a stamp regression), the derive branch (cmd_share.rs:827-888) would run instead. That branch also writes the cache and calls `record_remotes` with a document carrying the same `path.id`, so the assertions `remotes.len() == 1` and the key ending in `SERVER_PATH_ID` still pass. The cache branch's own record logic (it records under the caller's `session` with the stamp `fresh_cache_id` returned) is therefore untested.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1786},"end":{"line":1815},"content_hash":"4c312bd641cbeadabc1915d48628e1bbac37eb31bcfc57ee2b75281ab341331d"},"suggested_fix":"Between the two runs, overwrite the cache file with a document whose path has a different `path.id` (for example, rename it to `cached-only`), and have the mock server list only that id. Then only an upload of the cached body can produce the record. Also assert `remote.source_stamp` equals `stamp_string((rec.modified, rec.size))` of the manifest record.","summary":"`share_from_the_cache_records_the_upload` passes even if the share never takes the cache route","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:09:47.969796Z","id":"1cec24d88945b0af41961369fd63cd21538548b3ac7b4bf6e08de66cc1dee4d2","body":{"detail":"Every test that reaches `record_remotes` (cmd_export.rs tests `pathbase_export_of_a_cache_entry_records_against_its_session` and `pathbase_export_stamps_the_record_before_reading_the_body`, and the cmd_share.rs upload tests) uses a single-path document. `p export pathbase <cache id>` uploads whatever graph the cache entry holds, and that code path handles several inline paths, `$ref` entries (skipped), paths with no steps (skipped by `RemoteRecord::of`), and a server listing that omits a path or lists the paths in a different order. A regression to matching by position (`zip(inline, uploaded)`) would record the wrong server id under a path's key, or record a step-less path. With one path, such a regression is invisible.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":915},"end":{"line":957},"content_hash":"38f29feeece85216721f938b675d474ed720e67e520923413f4ebe541933d5c1"},"suggested_fix":"Add a unit test that calls `record_remotes` directly with a three-entry document: two inline paths with steps plus one `$ref`. Pass an `uploaded` list in reverse order that omits one of the inline paths. Assert that exactly one record is written, under the URL whose server id belongs to the listed path, with that path's `steps`/`last_step`.","summary":"`record_remotes` matches uploaded paths to document paths by `path.id`, but no test covers a document with more than one path","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:10:09.819872Z","id":"4222ffe0cce7acf29c2c9061f626ea8f4c71f53f73901feefa9150c9f32b3c93","body":{"detail":"In `run_pathbase_inner` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:1007-1028), the `AuthMode::Anon` branch returns `uploaded_paths(\"anon\", \"pathstash\", ...)`. Both `path share --anon` (cmd_share.rs:811-823 and :868-886) and `p export pathbase --anon <cache id>` (cmd_export.rs:891-896) then pass the result to `record_remotes`, which writes a `RemoteRecord` keyed `<server>/u/anon/pathstash/graphs/<g>/paths/<p>`. Anon graphs are created without auth on a rate-limited route that is not tied to any account (`anon_graphs_post`, crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs ~517-530), so no client can later append steps to that path. The record is documented as what incremental append and `share --all` will read (`RemoteRecord` doc, engine.rs ~55-62). Both readers will see a cursor saying the remote holds `steps` steps of the session, so they have to either special-case the magic owner string `anon` or will try appends that fail with 401/403. A later logged-in `share --all` could also take the session as already shared. The record shape carries no field saying the remote cannot be written.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1027},"end":{"line":1027},"content_hash":"95fb1776704a7ddc66bc20d5dd61205766477e76ae37b3cd691c196ce601c995"},"suggested_fix":"Skip `record_remotes` for `AuthMode::Anon` uploads (have `run_pathbase_inner` return an empty list, or a flag, on the anon branch) until a reader needs them. Or, if anon shares should be remembered, add a field to `RemoteRecord` saying the remote is read-only, so readers do not have to parse the owner out of the key.","summary":"Anonymous uploads write a remote record under owner `anon`, a graph the user has no credentials to append to, and nothing in the record says it was anonymous","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:10:09.819960Z","id":"24449c07fb63e479296ae3c74d4d9b6d9dc2d13aceb1522e1d16d5b7446f2405","body":{"detail":"`record_remotes` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:915-955) looks up each inline path with `uploaded.iter().find(|u| u.id == path.path.id)` (:941). Neither the client nor `Graph::from_json` checks that path ids are unique within a document. If a multi-path document repeats a `path.id`, both paths resolve to the first server id. `record_remote` replaces by URL (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs ~108-131), so the second path's `steps`/`last_step`/`head` overwrite the first's under the first path's URL, and the second server path gets no record. Both routes already return the paths in document order: the `POST /graphs` response documents `paths` as \"The stored paths in document order\" (crates/pathbase-client/openapi.json, GraphCreatedResponse.paths), and `stream_paths` pushes in document order (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs ~987-993). Matching by position would be unambiguous. This only matters if the server accepts duplicate path ids, which this repository does not show either way.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":938},"end":{"line":945},"content_hash":"58d7248e02b2ebc426f668fb643e24f955dce10b1f1d382f75313fab002c56fc"},"suggested_fix":"Pair the inline paths with `uploaded` by position (zip the inline paths with `uploaded` when the lengths match, and check `u.id == path.path.id` for each pair), and warn and record nothing when the lengths or ids disagree.","summary":"record_remotes matches uploaded paths to the server's list by `path.id`, so two inline paths that share an id both get the first server path's URL","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:05.484489Z","id":"f626e75824cb95a57b13919191f8390d88a2deb16e34b252f61c7d9256a82e32","body":{"detail":"`remote_path_url` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:75-105) formats `{server}/u/{owner}/{repo}/graphs/{graph}/paths/{path}`. Pathbase does not use that layout anywhere. Its graph URL, as the create response's `url` returns it, is `/u/<owner>/repos/<repo>/graphs/<uuid>` (the fixture in `graph_document_json`, cmd_pathbase.rs:1428, and the canonical form `extract_triple` documents at crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:452-454). Its API routes are `/api/v1/u/{owner}/repos/{repo}/graphs/{id}/paths/{path_id}` (crates/pathbase-client/openapi.json). The key leaves out `/repos/`. Fed back to path-cli's own parser (`parse_pathbase_ref` -> `extract_triple`, derive.rs:461-490), the key's segments are `[u, me, r, graphs, G, paths, P]`. The `/u/../repos/` branch does not match because segs[n-6] is `me`, not `u`. The `segs[n-2] == \"paths\"` branch then matches and returns owner=`graphs`, repo=`G`, id=`P`. So the docs at engine.rs:54-61, CLAUDE.md and CHANGELOG.md call the key 'the path's own URL', but it opens nothing and does not round-trip through the code that will read it. The rule that 'the containing graph is the key without its last two segments' gives `<server>/u/me/r/graphs/G`, which `extract_triple` does parse correctly but which Pathbase does not serve either. Nothing reads the key yet, so nothing fails today. But every record written from 0.30.0 on carries this spelling, so changing it later means migrating stored manifests.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":105},"content_hash":"0c4ad51dd0bd5f02872be672795ff88f4d6b705358f56a7a47e9b762b7c6d7ca"},"suggested_fix":"Build the key in the server's canonical form, `{server}/u/{owner}/repos/{repo}/graphs/{graph}/paths/{path}`, matching the `url` the create response returns. Teach `extract_triple` to accept and strip a trailing `/paths/<uuid>` (returning the path id too). Add a test that `parse_pathbase_ref(&remote_path_url(..))` gives back the same owner, repo and graph id. Update CLAUDE.md and the CHANGELOG entry to match.","summary":"remote_path_url builds a key that is neither a URL Pathbase serves nor one path-cli's own URL parser reads back: `extract_triple` turns it into owner \"graphs\", repo <graph uuid>, graph id <path uuid>","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:31.804551Z","id":"249f794ba260ad977ccb5f9877871e3fa1e13367877ab83d149181a229705471","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:1027 returns `uploaded_paths(\"anon\", \"pathstash\", &resp.id, &resp.paths)` from the AuthMode::Anon branch. crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:812-822 and :876-885 pass that result to `record_remotes` whatever the auth mode, and cmd_export.rs:891-896 does the same for `p export pathbase`. crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:523-530 calls `create_anon_graph` with no token. crates/pathbase-client/openapi.json:208 says the anon route creates the graph and its paths `frozen` (\"No authentication required ... The graph and its paths are created `frozen`\"), so later appends cannot succeed. RemoteRecord (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:63-74) has no field marking a remote as read-only. No reader exists yet (engine.rs:60-61), so concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"4222ffe0cce7acf29c2c9061f626ea8f4c71f53f73901feefa9150c9f32b3c93","summary":"confirmed: anon uploads return paths that callers record as remotes under owner anon, on a graph the server creates frozen","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:31.804564Z","id":"8423c4fc04519e6cea265e35ed7b0d5d80df52b99feb1e535af3a40cb9de7fdd","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:939-942 resolves each inline path with `uploaded.iter().find(|u| u.id == path.path.id)`, so a repeated id always gets the first match. `record_remote` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:108-131) inserts by URL, so the second record overwrites the first. One correction to the finding: the repo does show the server accepts duplicates. crates/pathbase-client/openapi.json UploadGraphBody (~line 2941) says \"the in-document toolpath path ID is a non-unique display/reference attribute, never a server key\". openapi.json:815 says `paths` is \"in document order, with the `path.id` it had in the document\", so pairing by position works. Session-derived docs have one path, so this is an edge case and suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"24449c07fb63e479296ae3c74d4d9b6d9dc2d13aceb1522e1d16d5b7446f2405","summary":"confirmed: matching by path.id gives repeated ids the first server path's URL, and the server spec says path ids are non-unique","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:12:13.318706Z","id":"71d2da364fc35fd7d75766d51d70035e7ef482dc761015421a278a89d1a11978","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:98-104 formats `{server}/u/{owner}/{repo}/graphs/{g}/paths/{p}`. Every API route in crates/pathbase-client/openapi.json is `/api/v1/u/{owner}/repos/{repo}/graphs/{id}/paths/{path_id}...`, and the create-response fixture at cmd_pathbase.rs:1428 is `https://pathbase.dev/u/alex/repos/pathstash/graphs/<uuid>`. crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:471-479 (extract_triple): for segs [u,me,r,graphs,G,paths,P] (n=7), segs[n-6]=`me` != `u` so the canonical branch fails; segs[n-2]=`paths` matches the second branch, returning owner=segs[3]=`graphs`, repo=segs[4]=G, id=P. Nothing reads the key yet (engine.rs:59-60 says so), so concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"f626e75824cb95a57b13919191f8390d88a2deb16e34b252f61c7d9256a82e32","summary":"confirmed: remote_path_url omits /repos/ and extract_triple misparses it as owner=graphs, repo=<graph uuid>","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:12:32.405405Z","id":"5d1a0a955003355c7e83d2f494f2a22d79bb97628c2872d10bd8ce9fc3873035","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:1786-1815 asserts only `rec.remotes.len() == 1` and that the key ends with `SERVER_PATH_ID`; it does not check stderr for `Cache is current` (cmd_share.rs:793-796) or otherwise distinguish branches. The derive branch (cmd_share.rs:827-888) rewrites the cache and calls `record_remotes` with `derived.doc` on `source.id`, and per the comment at cmd_share.rs:779-781 a derive reproduces the cached document byte-for-byte, so the same `path.id` (the one the mock lists) is uploaded and recorded under the same session `s1`. If `fresh_cache_id` returned `None`, the test would still pass; the cache branch's `record_remotes(harness, session, project, &doc, &uploaded, stamp)` (cmd_share.rs:814-823) is not pinned. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"8dc2b7a040e666ef7f911c551f6c2cd0a44b2701fb83d4c30b78a0b8363e54bc","summary":"confirmed: the test's assertions are equally satisfied by the derive branch","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:12:32.405416Z","id":"270a7ece17153874696f6481298ea11c5678a271a7c29b1309e2d3f00862c5ca","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:915-957 filters `$ref` entries, matches each inline path by `u.id == path.path.id`, and skips step-less paths via `RemoteRecord::of`. Callers in tests: cmd_export.rs:2201 and :2257 upload `make_path_doc()` (cmd_export.rs:1143, a single path `test-path`) with `graph_created_json(&[(\"test-path\", ...)])`; cmd_share.rs:1698, :1743, :1786 share a single Claude session (`doc.single_path()` at cmd_share.rs:1802). No test passes a multi-path document, a `$ref` entry, or an `uploaded` list in a different order or with omissions, so a positional-match regression would go unnoticed. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"1cec24d88945b0af41961369fd63cd21538548b3ac7b4bf6e08de66cc1dee4d2","summary":"confirmed: every test reaching record_remotes uses a one-path document","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T15:53:23.773863Z","id":"6cb47f591203732bdb2fc55ff35065163d7b74b9e638620b5cbee2c5721a5e15","body":{"detail":"Owner decision, 2026-10-13. The finding's diagnosis is half right. Pathbase's public URLs are /u/<owner>/<repo>/graphs/<id> and /u/<owner>/<repo>/paths/<id> with no /repos/ (pathbase crates/pathbase-api/src/responses.rs graph_url/path_url, and the web routes); the create response's url field is that form. Only the API routes carry /repos/. The path-cli fixture at cmd_pathbase.rs:1428 has claimed a /repos/ response URL since PR #66 and has never matched the server, so verifying against it is why the thread concluded /repos/ was missing. What is actually wrong: the current key mixes the browser graph URL with a nested /paths/<p> suffix the server does not serve anywhere, and path-cli's extract_triple misparses it. The CLI talks to the API, not the browser, so the key should be the path's API address: <server>/api/v1/u/<owner>/repos/<repo>/graphs/<g>/paths/<p>. That is a resource the server answers GET on, append is the key plus /steps, the graph needs no field because it is in the key, and the record shape stays remote-agnostic (for S3 the key is the object URL and the same read-here/push-here rule holds). A flat /paths/{id} API route on pathbase is a separate nice-to-have, not a prerequisite.","kind":"decision","references":"f626e75824cb95a57b13919191f8390d88a2deb16e34b252f61c7d9256a82e32","suggested_fix":"remote_path_url builds <server>/api/v1/u/<owner>/repos/<repo>/graphs/<g>/paths/<p> from the same parts the upload request used; teach extract_triple to accept that form (and return the path id) and tighten the greedy paths branch; fix the cmd_pathbase.rs:1428 fixture to the server's real response URL; add a test that parse_pathbase_ref(remote_path_url(..)) round-trips. Not implemented yet; lands in the #356 fix pass when approved.","summary":"Decided: key the record by the path's API resource URL, not a browser-shaped URL; the suggested fix of adding /repos/ to the current spelling is not the fix","tags":["review:pr-356-qual-2","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:10:26.155646Z","id":"2d3c5c16aaa80df2f28fc239adc543eea753a021656332846ba3a16543eb1d10","body":{"detail":"Owner decision, 2026-10-13. The record exists so the client can return to a path it owns and continue it. An anonymous upload is created frozen, is owned by nobody, and no credential ties it to this machine, so recording it claims a relationship that does not exist and forces every reader (append, share --all) to special-case the owner string. Consequences accepted: a session shared anonymously and later swept by an authed share --all is treated as new and uploaded under the user; append never sees an anon record; the record shape carries no anonymous flag and the owner string carries no meaning. Remembering anon share links for reprinting is upload history, a separate concern that does not belong in this record.","kind":"decision","references":"4222ffe0cce7acf29c2c9061f626ea8f4c71f53f73901feefa9150c9f32b3c93","suggested_fix":"In the share/export paths, skip record_remote when the upload was anonymous (owner anon / repo pathstash via the anon create route); add a test that an --anon share leaves remotes untouched. Not implemented yet; lands in the #356 fix pass.","summary":"Decided: anonymous uploads write no remote record at all","tags":["review:pr-356-qual-2","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:31:45.567057Z","id":"0b541f40b2635a4cbfb93df2048184d3dfdee5137ef63b924045538b6c332377","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Invalid: the format forbids this input. RFC.md:132: all path.id values must be unique within the graph. The finding's premise that ids need not be unique conflated the cross-graph rule (RFC.md:140) with the within-graph rule. Pairing by path.id is therefore correct for every valid document. That nothing validates uniqueness on ingest is a separate, pre-existing gap in toolpath Graph::from_json and the pathbase upload, not a #356 defect. Owner decision 2026-10-13.","supersedes":"24449c07fb63e479296ae3c74d4d9b6d9dc2d13aceb1522e1d16d5b7446f2405","tags":["reason:invalid","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T19:05:13.264941Z","id":"5c7ff79417ea518355ec205850c3350c1a72ce329cbe639346112a9c9fc9242e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f59b26e","summary":"Fixed on ben/remote-records in f59b26e: remote_path_url builds <server>/api/v1/u/<owner>/repos/<repo>/graphs/<g>/paths/<p>; extract_triple reads it with the path id and rejects route keywords/UUIDs as owner or repo; fixture at cmd_pathbase.rs:1428 is now /u/alex/pathstash/graphs/<id>. derive::tests::parse_pathbase_ref_round_trips_remote_path_url and parse_pathbase_ref_rejects_route_segments_as_names pass (cargo test -p path-cli: 510 passed).","supersedes":"f626e75824cb95a57b13919191f8390d88a2deb16e34b252f61c7d9256a82e32","tags":["review:pr-356-qual-2","reason:fixed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T19:05:13.536305Z","id":"19c797c6baa0e3acc87924a8201d5786dba037051cae3a0b6735cea13a48456d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:250cb12","summary":"Fixed in 250cb12: run_pathbase_inner returns None for an anonymous upload and share/export pathbase record nothing. cmd_share::tests::anon_share_leaves_remotes_untouched and cmd_export::tests::pathbase_anon_upload_names_no_path pass.","supersedes":"4222ffe0cce7acf29c2c9061f626ea8f4c71f53f73901feefa9150c9f32b3c93","tags":["review:pr-356-qual-2","reason:fixed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
